# Unrelated project folders living inside this repo dir — each with its own
# repo and its own secrets; never commit them, and server.mjs refuses to serve
# them. y3trading arrived this week at 240MB, ten thousand of those inside a
# .venv, one `git add -A` from a PUBLIC repo. Third of these in a few days
# (.library.json was TRACKED with a real shelf in it; airden/ sat untracked
# beside its own env file), so the rule: anything that lands next to the app
# and is not the app goes here the day it arrives.
21_questions/
y3trading/
.session_secret
.mind.json
.mind.json.tmp
.matches.json
.matches.json.tmp
.world.json
.world.json.tmp
.hull.json
.hull.json.tmp
.comments.json
.comments.json.tmp
test/.tmp-world/
.safety.json
.safety.json.tmp
.worn.json
.worn.json.tmp

# the inheritance: a private record, and the marker that says it landed
airden_*.json
.imported.json
.imported.json.tmp
.patterns.json
.patterns.json.tmp

# A PRESENCE'S SHELF IS DATA, NOT CODE. .library.json was tracked, and 25KB of a
# real shelf went to a public repo with it. Production never reads the tracked
# copy (DATA_DIR=/data there) — only local dev did — so untracking costs nothing
# and closes the path where a local --go run would publish imported private work.
# (The already-committed copy stays in history; untracking stops the next write.)
.library.json
.library.json.tmp
